PulseAudio drops any block larger than a record stream's max_length, so a source with fixed
blocks never delivers data and play(), which waits for the first bytes, never returns.
Serein's 20 ms buffer is smaller than the blocks of a sink monitor and of module-sles-source.

--- a/src/host/pulseaudio/mod.rs
+++ b/src/host/pulseaudio/mod.rs
@@ -647,7 +647,9 @@
             protocol::stream::BufferAttr {
                 // fragment_size controls the delivery chunk size for record
                 // streams; target_length is playback-only and is ignored here.
-                max_length: len,
+                // Sources with fixed blocks post several fragments at once, and a
+                // smaller queue would discard every block.
+                max_length: len.saturating_mul(8),
                 fragment_size: len,
                 ..Default::default()
             }
